diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..b49467f 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,56 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Deliveries
+
+When an event a webhook is subscribed to happens on its board, Fizzy sends a `POST` request to the webhook's payload URL. Every event is delivered to a webhook exactly once: there are no retries, and a delivery is never repeated.
+
+__Request headers:__
+
+| Header | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `User-Agent` | `fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook` |
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json` (or `text/html` for Campfire) |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | When the request was sent, as an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | Hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the request body, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret` |
+
+Verify a request by computing the HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body with the signing secret and comparing it to the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+__Request body:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb",
+    "number": 1,
+    "title": "The logo isn't big enough",
+    "status": "published",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/1"
+  },
+  "board": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy",
+    "name": "Fizzy",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/boards/03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy"
+  },
+  "creator": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7",
+    "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`eventable` is a [card](cards.md) or a [comment](comments.md), depending on the action. `board` and `creator` have the same shape as elsewhere in the API; abbreviated above.
+
+Webhooks whose payload URL points at Slack, Campfire, or a Basecamp Campfire chat receive a short chat message describing the event instead of the JSON above.
+
+__Outcomes:__
+
+A delivery is `completed` when the receiver answered. It counts as a success only when the answer was a `2xx` status. Redirects are not followed. When the receiver could not be reached, or did not answer within 10 seconds, the delivery is `errored` and `response.error` says why: `destination_unreachable`, `timeout`, `ssl_error`, or `invalid_response`.
+
+A receiver that keeps failing gets switched off: after ten failed deliveries in a row, with the first of them at least an hour ago, the webhook is deactivated and no more deliveries are made until it is [reactivated](#post-account_slugboardsboard_idwebhooksidactivation). A successful delivery resets the count.
+
+The delivery log is kept for a week.
